{
  "module": "Attention: how tokens exchange information",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "causal-mask",
    "title": "The causal mask",
    "summary": "How attention is stopped from looking at later tokens: the lower-triangular mask, why it is applied to the scores before softmax, and why training needs it.",
    "covers": ["causal-mask", "mask-in-training"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "scores-weights",
        "reason": "The mask edits the scores that become the weights."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "logits-softmax",
        "reason": "It works through softmax renormalising over the allowed positions."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "teacher-forcing",
        "reason": "It matters most in the setting where whole sequences are fed at once."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "As described so far, every position can attend to "
            },
            {
              "text": "every",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " position, including the ones that come after it. But a model that generates text must predict a token "
            },
            {
              "text": "without seeing the future",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So attention has to be restricted: position i may use only the tokens up to and including i."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 41)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "the-mask",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The restriction is the "
            },
            {
              "text": "causal mask",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", a lower-triangular pattern: position i may attend to positions j ≤ i only."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/schematics/transformer-causal-mask.svg",
          "alt": "Causal attention mask for five tokens, The cat sat on mat. A lower-triangular grid of queries against keys: each query may attend to itself and earlier tokens, and every later position is marked minus infinity. After softmax the minus infinity entries become 0.",
          "display": "expandable"
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 41)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "how",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It is applied to the "
            },
            {
              "text": "scores",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", before softmax: every score S_ij with j > i is set to "
            },
            {
              "text": "−∞",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Take query 2 of the toy case, with scores 0, 1, 1. The third key is in the future, so the scores become 0, 1, −∞."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Now "
            },
            {
              "text": "exp(−∞) = 0",
              "code": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", so softmax gives 0.269, 0.731, 0.000: the future position gets weight exactly 0, and the other weights still add up to 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 41, 42)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "before-not-after",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Why not just softmax first, and then zero the future weights? Because then the row no longer adds up to 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Query 2 without a mask has weights 0.155, 0.422, 0.422. Zeroing the third leaves 0.155, 0.422, 0.000, which add up to only about 0.58. That is not a proper weighted average."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Masking the scores first lets softmax "
            },
            {
              "text": "renormalise over the allowed positions",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " automatically."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 43)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "in-training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "In generation there are no future tokens anyway, so why is the mask needed in "
            },
            {
              "text": "training",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Because training feeds the "
            },
            {
              "text": "whole sequence at once",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and every position predicts its own next token in parallel. Without the mask, position i could read token i + 1, which is exactly its label, and simply learn to copy it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 44)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "same-computation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The mask has a second benefit. It makes each position's result "
            },
            {
              "text": "independent of later tokens",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", so training and generation compute the same thing for a given position."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Without that, a model trained one way would behave differently when used the other way."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 44)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What does the causal mask do?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It lets position i attend only to positions j ≤ i: itself and earlier tokens"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Later positions are blocked."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It lets every position attend to every other position"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is attention without a mask."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It hides the earlier tokens from position i"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It is the later tokens that are hidden."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It removes tokens from the vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The mask acts on attention scores, not on the vocabulary."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
